# gstack — Virtual Engineering Team

gstack provides structured review and QA skills adapted from Garry Tan's software factory.
Skills live at `~/.cursor/skills/gstack/` and each subdirectory contains a `SKILL.md`.

## Available Skills

| Skill | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `plan-ceo-review` | Rethink the problem, find the 10-star product |
| `plan-eng-review` | Lock architecture, data flow, edge cases, tests |
| `plan-design-review` | 80-item design audit with letter grades, AI slop detection |
| `design-consultation` | Build a complete design system from scratch |
| `review` | Pre-landing PR review: SQL safety, trust boundaries, completeness |
| `ship` | Sync main, run tests, audit coverage, push, open PR |
| `browse` | Headless Chromium browser for QA (~100ms/command) |
| `qa` | Test app, find bugs, fix with atomic commits, regression tests |
| `qa-only` | Same as qa but report-only, no code changes |
| `qa-design-review` | Design audit that fixes what it finds |
| `setup-browser-cookies` | Import cookies from real browser into headless session |
| `retro` | Weekly retro with per-person breakdowns and trends |
| `document-release` | Update all project docs to match shipped changes |

## How to Use in Cursor

When a user mentions a gstack skill by name (e.g. "run a review", "do a CEO review",
"QA this page"), read `~/.cursor/skills/gstack/{skill-name}/SKILL.md` and follow its
instructions. Adapt Claude Code-specific references:

- `AskUserQuestion` → use natural language questions in your response
- `Bash` → use the Shell tool
- `$B <command>` → `~/.claude/skills/gstack/browse/dist/browse <command>`

## Browse Binary

The gstack headless browser is available at:
`~/.claude/skills/gstack/browse/dist/browse`

Use it via Shell for QA testing, screenshots, and page interaction.

## Completeness Principle

gstack follows the "Boil the Lake" principle: always do the complete thing when AI
makes the marginal cost near-zero. Prefer the complete implementation over shortcuts.
